    "title": "pandas.Series.items — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.items#\n\n- Series.items()[source]#\n- Lazily iterate over (index, value) tuples. This method returns an iterable tuple (index, value). This is convenient if you want to create a lazy iterator. \n  - Returns:\n    - iterable\n    - Iterable of tuples containing the (index, value) pairs from a Series.\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.items`\n  - Iterate over (column name, Series) pairs.\n  - `DataFrame.iterrows`\n  - Iterate over DataFrame rows as (index, Series) pairs.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series(['A', 'B', 'C']) >>> for index, value in s.items(): ... print(f\"Index : {index}, Value : {value}\") Index : 0, Value : A Index : 1, Value : B Index : 2, Value : C",
